<title>SINGAPORE: Singatronics to buy New Zealand Hotel.</title>
<headline>Singatronics to buy New Zealand Hotel.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singatronics Ltd said on Friday it has entered into an agreement with Tower Corp of New Zeland to acquire a hotel in Auckland for NZ$28.2 million.</p>
<p>It said the hotel is known as Auckland Airport Travelodge and is located near the Auckland international airport.</p>
<p>Singatronics said the purchase is supported by the hotel's historical earnings and a forecast net operating profit before interest, depreciation and taxation of NZ$3.9 million.</p>
<p>The hotel, on freehold land of approximately 3.81 hectares, has 243 guest rooms.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom 65-8703080</p>
